Probe the CPU's SIMD support once per process instead of once per object.

libjpeg-turbo 3.1.90 moved the SIMD dispatcher's answer from a thread-local
into each compress and decompress object ("Overhaul SIMD dispatchers",
https://github.com/libjpeg-turbo/libjpeg-turbo/commit/ced602ad2f), because
thread-local storage can fail on Windows
(https://github.com/libjpeg-turbo/libjpeg-turbo/issues/834). Before the
thread-local it was a plain global, which was a data race
(https://github.com/libjpeg-turbo/libjpeg-turbo/issues/87).

Since 3.1.90 every object calls jpeg_simd_cpu_support(). On x86-64 that is
three CPUID instructions and one XGETBV, and under a hypervisor each CPUID is a
VM exit of about 2 us. 3.1.4 and earlier asked once for each thread. Bun makes
a new object for every JPEG decode and encode.

This patch keeps the answer in a process-wide static. It uses no thread-local
storage, and the atomic builtins leave no data race. They are clang and GCC
builtins, which is why this is a local patch. The per-object fields and the
JSIMD_FORCE* / JSIMD_NOHUFFENC environment overrides stay as they are. Only
the raw CPU answer is shared.

--- a/simd/jsimd.c
+++ b/simd/jsimd.c
@@ -48,6 +48,27 @@
 #endif
 
 
+/*
+ * Bun: jpeg_simd_cpu_support() runs CPUID three times on x86, and CPUID is a
+ * VM exit under a hypervisor (about 2 us each).  Every new compress or
+ * decompress object used to call it.  The answer cannot change, so keep it for
+ * the process.  Threads that race on the first call each probe and store the
+ * same value, so nothing waits.  JSIMD_UNDEFINED is never a probe result.
+ */
+LOCAL(unsigned int)
+simd_cpu_support_once(void)
+{
+  static unsigned int cached = JSIMD_UNDEFINED;
+  unsigned int simd_support = __atomic_load_n(&cached, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST);
+
+  if (simd_support == JSIMD_UNDEFINED) {
+    simd_support = jpeg_simd_cpu_support();
+    __atomic_store_n(&cached, simd_support, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST);
+  }
+  return simd_support;
+}
+
+
 /*
  * Check what SIMD accelerations are supported.
  */
@@ -67,7 +88,7 @@ init_simd(j_common_ptr cinfo)
   if (simd_support != JSIMD_UNDEFINED)
     return;
 
-  simd_support = jpeg_simd_cpu_support();
+  simd_support = simd_cpu_support_once();
 
 #ifndef NO_GETENV
   /* Force different settings through environment variables */
